{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The equation is in *slope-intercept form*, $y=mx+b$.\n\nIn this form, $b$ gives the $y$-intercept.\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"The **$y$-intercept** is the point of the graph on the $y$-axis, which happens when $x=0$.\n\nLet's plug in $x=0$ and see what happens.\n\n$\\begin{align}\ny\u0026=mx+b\\\\\\\\\ny\u0026=m(0)+b\\\\\\\\\ny\u0026=b\n\\end{align}$\n\nSo $b$ gives us the $y$-intercept.","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Why?","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"The $y$-intercept of $y=-3x+\\greenD{0}$ is $(0,\\greenD{0})$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**What is the $y$-intercept of $y=-3x$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$(0,0)$","correct":true},{"content":"$(-3,0)$","correct":false},{"content":"$(-3,-3)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$(0,-3)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
